    "key_findings": [
      "The proposed copula-based pairs trading strategy on cointegrated cryptocurrency pairs outperforms both Bitcoin buy-and-hold and portfolio buy-and-hold benchmark strategies in profitability and risk-adjusted returns.",
      "Using lower entry thresholds (e.g., alpha_1 = 0.10) decreases volatility and increases returns concurrently, whereas higher thresholds lead to increased number of transactions and higher volatility without a corresponding return increase.",
      "Extreme value copulas (such as Tawn type 1 and 2) and certain two-parameter Archimedean copulas (particularly BB7) play a significant role in modeling cryptocurrency pair dependencies.",
      "Both the linear Engle-Granger (EG) and non-linear Kapetanios-Shin-Snell (KSS) cointegration tests yield comparable risk-adjusted performance at the optimal threshold level."
